        "slide": 1,
        "slideId": "s1",
        "speaker": "Dr. Nova",
        "text": "Welcome to Lesson 1.7, the capstone architectural module of Track 1: Dataset Management, Governance, and Lifecycle Architecture. Across industry and biomedical research, the longevity and legal credibility of an artificial intelligence system depend strictly on its data infrastructure: who may read sensitive fields, which cryptographic snapshot trained a model, how backups survive disaster, and how erasure mandates are obeyed.",
