        "slide": 2,
        "slideId": "s2",
        "speaker": "Dr. Nova",
        "text": "As Sculley and colleagues demonstrated at NeurIPS 2015, machine learning systems accumulate hidden technical debt primarily through unmanaged data dependencies. Unlike source code guarded by Git commits, datasets stored on ad-hoc shared network drives suffer silent corruption.",
