        "text": "Because systemic access and insurance barriers caused health systems to spend far less on Black patients than white patients with identical chronic disease burdens, Black patients had to be drastically sicker to reach the same dollar risk score. Replacing expenditure with active biomarkers like HbA1c and chronic condition counts eliminated the gap, boosting qualified Black patient enrollment by 84 percent.",
