        "speaker": "Dr. Nova",
        "text": "Active Checkpoint 1: The 1-10-100 Cost Cascade Arithmetic. Let's test your financial and mathematical comprehension of quality cascade modeling. Suppose an enterprise ingestion pipeline processes 5,000,000 records monthly with a 0.5% corruption rate, generating 25,000 corrupt records. Upstream validation costs $0.05 per record; warehouse cleaning costs $0.50 per record; and production billing repair costs $5.00 per record. If 20% of corrupt records leak past the warehouse into customer billing, calculate the net monthly financial savings of deploying upstream pre-ingestion validation. Select the correct option below.",
