        "text": "Third, Asia-Pacific emphasizes state sovereignty and cross-border security assessments under China's PIPL—imposing penalties up to fifty million RMB, five percent annual revenue, and operating license revocation—alongside Singapore's PDPA. Notice across Table 3.7 how de-identification thresholds, cross-border mechanisms, and private rights of action diverge structurally across jurisdictions.",
