        "slideId": "s3",
        "speaker": "Dr. Nova",
        "text": "Notice the sigmoid parameterization: P of y-w preferred over y-l equals sigma of the reward difference r of y-w minus r of y-l. In classical RLHF, teams trained a separate neural network reward model r-psi by minimizing negative log-likelihood. But training this reward model alongside an actor policy and reference model created immense PPO instability.",
