        "slide": 4,
        "slideId": "s4",
        "speaker": "Dr. Nova",
        "text": "When we take the logarithm and rearrange for the reward r, the intractable partition function beta ln Z of x appears. But look at what happens when we substitute r into the Bradley-Terry preference difference: beta ln Z of x is identical for both completions, so it cancels out completely! This yields the exact DPO loss, optimized using standard cross-entropy gradients.",
