        "slide": 10,
        "slideId": "s10",
        "speaker": "Dr. Nova",
        "text": "Slide 10 presents the fundamental limit of synthetic dataset generation: the Recursive Model Collapse Theorem, published by Shumailov and colleagues in Nature in 2024. Suppose an initial dataset D-zero has variance sigma-squared-zero. If generation n plus 1 is trained recursively on samples generated by generation n, what happens?",
